,"caption":"Canyon Run","poi_name":"Elephant Buttress Rapid","subject":"Lower half of Elephant Buttress Rapid","author":"Brian Adkins","poi_id":"103634","photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/20","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/20"}},{"id":"NoO69QtSdSxCsxcHZIjAj","ext":"jpg","post_id":"SmqxFcNRwzEeE1Cpp1JHA","description":"250 cfs","caption":"Third drop.","poi_name":null,"subject":"Elephant Buttress","author":"Dejan Smaic","poi_id":"103634","photo_date":"2021-06-30T14:44:21.000Z","updated_at":"2021-07-02T14:44:21.000Z","url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/NoO69QtSdSxCsxcHZIjAj","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/NoO69QtSdSxCsxcHZIjAj"}},{"id":"rST4mtSfzh8zyNWgCKs3w","ext":"jpg","post_id":"rST4mtSfzh8zyNWgCKs3w","description":"Add a Caption","caption":"432cfs","poi_name":null,"subject":"432cfs","author":"MaxwellBoice34","poi_id":null,"photo_date":"2021-06-16T18:23:00.000Z","updated_at":"2021-06-17T00:24:46.000Z","url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/rST4mtSfzh8zyNWgCKs3w","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/rST4mtSfzh8zyNWgCKs3w"}},{"id":"ePXWUPGYAPZo8YweOyWEe","ext":"jpg","post_id":"p5KilgvdcEnwxD5TLuh9e","description":null,"caption":"Boulder Creek @04. Blue Bridge to Eben G Fine Park","poi_name":null,"subject":null,"author":"Dejan Smaic","poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":"2021-12-26T12:06:49.000Z","url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/ePXWUPGYAPZo8YweOyWEe","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/ePXWUPGYAPZo8YweOyWEe"}},{"id":"09bj5qNaUWfhCzbKbNe2B","ext":"jpg","post_id":"CPgF5nNRi97ebPkqb99I7","description":null,"caption":"Bryce entering the runout","poi_name":null,"subject":"Elephant Buttress","author":"Dejan Smaic","poi_id":null,"photo_date":"2021-07-02T12:08:09.000Z","updated_at":"2021-12-26T12:08:09.000Z","url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/09bj5qNaUWfhCzbKbNe2B","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/09bj5qNaUWfhCzbKbNe2B"}},{"id":"avyqxtMC1s8xQ5U8J1yRl","ext":"jpg","post_id":"Z5U7l4dnmq2K08hJkquLt","description":null,"caption":"Bryce taking the left line of the second drop","poi_name":null,"subject":"Elephant Buttress - 2nd Drop","author":"Dejan Smaic","poi_id":null,"photo_date":"2021-07-02T17:04:38.000Z","updated_at":"2021-12-26T17:04:38.000Z","url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/avyqxtMC1s8xQ5U8J1yRl","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/avyqxtMC1s8xQ5U8J1yRl"}}],"detail":{"id":"364","permitUrl":"","permitInfo":"","description":"With fun streambed gradient Middle Boulder Creek surprises the first time boater with its friendly nature and so many read and run rapids.\n\nThe bridge at the Red Lion Inn has been a challenge at various flood events.\n\nThe culverts filled up with wood and the bridge has previously washed away. Also there are two low-head dams near the diversion tunnels, but they are runnable.\n\nBelow the first pedestrian bridge, at Elephant Buttress, there is a reasonably fun play hole.\n\n**Elephant Buttress Rapid** (IV+).\n\nUpdated 2021:  The Buttress section was modified in 2019/2020 due to post-2013 flood reconstruction.  This section is considered a Class IV during normal flows, and consists of 3 distinct drops and a long channelized runout. The second drop is worth a scout as the line goes left, and the hydraulics can make for an interesting day at higher flows. The run out is channelized, fast, and consists of blast rock.  Swimmers through this section have come out battered. Video Link of Elephant Buttress at 250 cfs:  _**[Elephant Buttress Video @ 250 cfs](https://youtu.be/soFPC1dTWfE)**_\n\nPre-2019 Description:  If you haven't been down this rapid before it is worth a scout. Being a roadblasted mank zone, its a bad place to be upside down.\n\nShortly downstream, after passing under two road bridges, prepare to negotiate a wier from river right.\n\nThe whitewater course at Eben G. Fine Park is one of the first of its kind in design. It has a few spin holes and eddy lines. A trashy ender hole called Widowmaker is located at the end of the course, just past the Arapahoe Street bridge.\n\nFloods of September 2013 have significantly changed the streambed of Middle Boulder Creek. Newly incised channels within this watershed have changed stream channel character, debris pile movement will be in flux while man-made obstacles and structural abandonments may be present in this stream channel.\n\nSee _Colorado Rivers and Creeks II_, by Banks and Eckardt _(The Bible)_, for info on this and most of the other kewl runs of Colorado.\n\nLat/longitude coords are approximate, from TopoZone.\n\nThe various reaches of Boulder Creek,\n\n[Jasper Creek](http://www.americanwhitewater.org/content/River/view/river-detail/4267/) (Class V+/VI),\n\n[The Source](http://www.americanwhitewater.org/content/River/view/river-detail/3360/) (Class V),\n\n[Upper Boulder Canyon](http://www.americanwhitewater.org/content/River/view/river-detail/4223/) (Class V/V+),\n\n[Lower Boulder Canyon](http://www.americanwhitewater.org/content/River/view/river-detail/364/) (Class IV),\n\n[Boulder Town Run](http://www.americanwhitewater.org/content/River/view/river-detail/2881/) (Class II/III),\n\n[North Fork Boulder](http://www.americanwhitewater.org/content/River/view/river-detail/4224/) (Class V+/VI),\n\n[Alto-Alto](http://www.americanwhitewater.org/content/River/view/river-detail/4238/) (Class IV),\n\n[Upper South Boulder](http://www.americanwhitewater.org/content/River/view/river-detail/3125/) (Class V+/VI),\n\n[Lower South Boulder](http://www.americanwhitewater.org/content/River/view/river-detail/2883/) (Class IV/V+/VI),\n\n[Eldorado Canyon](http://www.americanwhitewater.org/content/River/view/river-detail/3453/) (Class V+).","averageGradient":"136","maxGradient":"220","length":"3.8","correlations":[{"reachID":"364","isPrimary":true,"correlationDetails":{"metric":"cfs","belowRecommendedRangeComment":null,"lowRunnableRangeComment":null,"mediumRunnableRangeComment":null,"highRunnableRangeComment":null,"aboveRecommendedRangeComment":null,"lowRunnableAdjustedDifficulty":null,"highRunnableAdjustedDifficulty":null,"beginLowRunnable":"150","beginMediumRunnable":null,"beginHighRunnable":null,"endHighRunnable":"1000"},"gaugeInfo":{"name":"BOULDER CREEK NEAR ORODELL, CO.","gaugeSource":"COLORADO_DEPARTMENT_OF_WATER_RESOURCES","gaugeSourceIdentifier":"BOCOROCO","gaugeFetchStatus":"ACTIVE","latestFlowReading":{"value":"58","dateTime":"2026-05-11T02:15:00.000Z","qualifier":"NORMAL"},"latestStageReading":{"value":"2.16","dateTime":"2026-05-11T02:15:00.000Z","qualifier":"NORMAL"},"location":{"latitude":"40.006534","longitude":"-105.330525"},"externalSourceLinks":null},"migrationErrorExplanation":null,"comment":null,"status":{"status":"stale","latestReading":{"value":"58","dateTime":"2026-05-11T02:15:00.000Z","qualifier":"NORMAL"},"metric":"cfs","adjustedDifficulty":null}}],"pointOfInterestIDs":["103634","110755","116024"],"geometry":{"type":"LineString","coordinates":[[-105.339,40.005795],[-105.338916,40.005797],[-105.338544,40.005786],[-105.338301,40.005742],[-105.338116,40.005687],[-105.337851,40.005522],[-105.337666,40.005352],[-105.337594,40.005253],[-105.337487,40.005022],[-105.337401,40.004896],[-105.337273,40.004825],[-105.337123,40.004775],[-105.336901,40.004775],[-105.336665,40.004797],[-105.336444,40.00483],[-105.336323,40.004836],[-105.336137,40.004864],[-105.335966,40.004902],[-105.335523,40.005023],[-105.33508,40.005193],[-105.334923,40.005232],[-105.334816,40.005237],[-105.334744,40.005232],[-105.334716,40.005199],[-105.33468,40.005072],[-105.334651,40.004985],[-105.334637,40.004919],[-105.334551,40.004798],[-105.334316,40.004562],[-105.334109,40.004435],[-105.333916,